# fixedbugs, defect 2052, 2026-10-13, the reproducer.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own calling `hero_str_le`, a function
# nobody declared, built: the header's region ignored `-Wall`, and with it
# clang's default error for an implicit declaration, so the build stopped
# at the link, `internal error: linking failed`, exit 2.
#
# FIX: `-Wimplicit-function-declaration` stays an error in the region
# (`emit/header_region.hero`'s `KEPT`), the header refused at the call's
# line 4, exit 1, and clang's suggestion, a note of its own at the call,
# told as the Heroes runtime's own name (`cli/runtime_name.hero`).

extern "fixedbugs-2052-a-header-that-calls-a-misspelled-runtime-function-is-refused.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function eight() -> i32

function main()
    print(eight())
